# The same gears, out of the same billet, by a completely different machine.
#
# No furnace, no burner, no coal, no rolling mill and no press: a lathe takes
# cold billet straight from the inlet and cuts gears out of it. Ten components
# instead of thirteen, on a third of the plot, and nothing is burned.
#
# What it costs is throughput, grid power and metal. Twenty billet a tick
# becomes twelve gears and eight swarf, so two fifths of the iron leaves in the
# skip -- and the gears that do come out are cut rather than stamped, which is
# the one thing this brief does not ask for and the reason stamping wins it.

machine "Machining Cell"
brief gears

inlet     I1  at 0,0   draws iron
lathe     L1  at 4,0
lathe     L2  at 4,3
outlet    O1  at 9,0
skip      SK1 at 9,4

cable     CB1 at 0,4
mains     M1  at 0,7
motor     MO1 at 4,7
motor     MO2 at 7,7

wire I1.out -> L1.in
wire I1.out -> L2.in

wire M1.power -> CB1.in
wire M1.power -> MO1.power
wire M1.power -> MO2.power
wire CB1.out -> L1.power
wire CB1.out -> L2.power
wire MO1.rotary -> L1.drive
wire MO2.rotary -> L2.drive

wire L1.out -> O1.solid
wire L2.out -> O1.solid
wire L1.swarf -> SK1.solid
wire L2.swarf -> SK1.solid
